  "body": "The batch gate on `main` bdf17d8a (2026-11-11, `gate-logs/batch-20261111-224322/02-cl_suites.log`) fails one test:\n\n```\ntest cl_bin_prints_move_stats ... FAILED\npanicked at crates\\cl\\tests\\headless_bin.rs:49:5\nmoves: 69 (rapid 12, feed 51, plunge 6, arcs 33)\n```\n\n`crates/cl/tests/headless_bin.rs:49` asserts `moves: 69 (rapid 12, feed 51, plunge 6, arcs 30)` for `crates/app/tests/golden/contour_disc_hole.cl`. PR #839 (merged as 575f02d8, arc fitting) changed that golden - the same 69 moves, 33 of them arcs now - and its reviews accepted the golden change, but this count in the cl crate was not updated: the cl suite reads a golden that lives under `crates/app/tests`, and neither the PR's gate nor its reviews ran the cl suites (the coverage hole #922 / #925 describe).\n\nNot wrong output: a stale test expectation. Fix: update the expected line to `arcs 33` after confirming against the golden that 33 is what #839 intended (its decision file and review explain the plateau and lead-out arcs), and nothing else in that line changed.\n\nDone means: `cargo test -p camcraft-cl --test headless_bin` passes on main; the PR body names #839 as the merge that changed the golden.\n",
